-- 4200 (release 50; docs/releases/r50.md): the Academy gets two upgrades.
--  1. Every multiple-choice question carries ONE extra, obviously wrong, funny answer option (light workplace humour about
--     cars, renters, Toronto traffic and coffee). The bank of jokes is web/src/features/academy/jokes.json (generated into
--     app.academy_joke_bank below by supabase/seed/4200_gen_academy.mjs). A before insert or update trigger on academy_questions
--     adds one joke at a pseudo-random position when a question has none, and moves the index of the right answer with it, so the
--     right answer stays the same option. It also catches a question a later migration, a generator or an Admin saves again
--     with the plain options: the joke comes back by itself. A joke is never the right answer; picking it is simply wrong.
--  2. Every section gets a last lesson, "See it", of pictures: screens with numbered pins, good and bad example photos, flow
--     diagrams, Do and Do not pairs and icon lists (supabase/seed/academy/r50visuals.mjs; the pictures are webp files in
--     web/public/academy). SCHEMA_MARKER 4200.

-- ================================================================ 1. up to seven options (six and the joke)
alter table academy_questions drop constraint if exists academy_questions_options_check;
alter table academy_questions add constraint academy_questions_options_check
  check (jsonb_typeof(options) = 'array' and jsonb_array_length(options) between 2 and 7);

